I'm at the point where it makes sense to combine the .db files into a
single file.  That's 4 files into 1.  The in-memory representation
needs to remain the same, but there's no reason I can't store all of
the data in a single file.  This simplifies mkcurtaindb as well as
the server code in mccurtaind.

How did I get here in the first place?

  Way back when, I was focused on the in-memory representation for
  reasonably fast lookups.  Hence the separation of the prefixes->ASes
  and ASes->prefixes mappings, as well as the AS->name mappings.  I
  also didn't have IPv6 support, so I had 2 database files instead of
  4.

  Another primary reason: the ASes->prefixes mappings can be created
  from the prefixes->ASes, and vice versa.  Neither representation is
  very friendly for aggregation; they're designed for lookup.  So the
  routeviews data gets its own representation that we use for
  aggregation (while creating the databases).

If I assume I always write all 4 of the mappings and always in the
same order, this isn't difficult.  But I should probably create
a free funtion or a class to encapsulate the 4 mappings, and possibly
also the AS->name mappings.  While I need 2 routeviews files plus
asn.txt to create what I need on the server, I could store my data
in a single file.